{
  "story": "How does a tree choose a threshold? Start with samples sorted by feature value. Test each midpoint between neighboring values, preserving every sample. Compare the child class counts and size-weighted Gini impurity. Finally, return to the lowest-scoring cut: a winning split can still leave one child mixed.",
